Description: Tools for reading Trends in International Mathematics and Science
    Study (TIMSS) international database files stored in R format
    <https://timss2023.org/data/>, merging the student questionnaire and student
    achievement files, and preparing questionnaire variables (missing-value
    codes, reversed agreement scales and yes/no items). The package also fits
    a multiple linear regression of the average of the five plausible values
    on selected predictors, reporting standardized coefficients, correlations
    and variance inflation factors, and provides heteroscedasticity diagnostics
    (Breusch-Pagan test and HC3 robust standard errors). Sampling weights and
    replicate weights are not applied; for design-based estimation see the
    packages 'intsvy' and 'RALSA'.
